From ca3a47e124cbeba08a0e3f33c7d33eeccc453c2d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andre Watson <dre@ligandal.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 23:46:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 22/32] test(qsa): pin the shared-scratch allocation plan and
 its byte budget

CPU only, no device needed. Drives the production plan object and the production
row-sizing helpers, and reads production source for the two things already shared
(the graph memory pool, the logits output buffer) so a regression there fails here
rather than in a boot.

Pins: one allocation serves every tier with a stable base pointer; a reservation
made at the deepest width covers every shallower tier in the exact order the
adaptive controller builds them; a late reservation that would grow an allocated
buffer raises; an over-capacity request returns None rather than reallocating; k
and v do not alias; and the B3c-4 byte budget (20 instances, 2560 MiB of workspace
and 234 MiB of gather buffers unshared vs 128 + 36 shared; 2219 MiB recovered
across the three extra tiers, 87394 KV tokens at 26 KB).

18 pass in the serving venv, 16 pass + 2 skip in a plain test venv
(the two cases that import the engine need the serving venv transformers build).
